  "symptom": "The unattended-run stop guard counts things as typed by the user that nobody typed, and misses one that was. Wrongly counted as typed: a compaction summary Claude Code writes after the context fills, an entry that is only shown in the transcript, and a skill loaded inside a subagent (a sidechain), which also should not start or end a run. Wrongly not counted: a slash command the user types in the middle of the run. After finish, a task notification should not count as the user speaking either.",
